new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fd2c437
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** A successful `get` never moved the key to
+   the most-recently-used end of the `OrderedDict`, so a freshly read entry was
+   still evicted as least-recently-used. Fixed by calling
+   `self._data.move_to_end(key)` on a cache hit (per the docstring, both `get`
+   and `put` count as "use").
+
+2. **`put` evicted before checking whether the key already existed.** Updating
+   an existing key in a full cache first popped the oldest entry, even though
+   the update adds no new entry and should evict nothing. Fixed by only
+   evicting when the key is not already present
+   (`if key not in self._data and len(self._data) >= self.capacity`).
